<h2>What is ChatGPT?</h2>
<p>ChatGPT is an AI and machine learning-powered model developed from OpenAI, a leading artificial intelligence research devwp. It uses natural language processing (NLP) and deep learning to generate human-like responses to conversations in an intelligent manner.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>ChatGPT has been trained on millions of conversation examples worldwide, allowing it to understand how humans communicate and respond accordingly.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The popularity has skyrocketed, especially for chatbots and virtual assistants. Since ChatGPT is programmed to comprehend and interpret human language, it may provide responses virtually identical to those of a human being.</p>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Screenshot-2023-03-29-at-5.11.11-PM.png" alt="chatgpt features"></p>
<h3>The Technology Behind ChatGPT</h3>
<p>Open AI ChatGPT is a natural language understanding (NLU) system based on the <strong>Transformer architecture</strong>. It was trained on a large amount of text data using unsupervised learning. This means it did not get explicit instructions about what to learn but instead discovered patterns and relationships independently.</p>
<p>To produce an appropriate response, it uses the knowledge to produce an understandable response through a cohesive step-by-step process. Open AI ChatGPT’s capacity to produce natural and human-like language is one of its advantages. It enables the model to comprehend the context and provide answers suitable for the particular circumstance.</p>
<p>Note: ChatGPT’s <a href="https://help.openai.com/en/articles/6827058-why-doesn-t-chatgpt-know-about-x">data cut-off is at 2021</a>. This can be an explanation to why ChatGPT may not know about recent trends or news.</p>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Screenshot-2023-03-29-at-5.18.45-PM.png" alt="chatgpt data"></p>
<p>Even though the cut-off date is 2021, ChatGPT has the capability to come up with accurate responses based on its training data. Its living proof is a recent story on how ChatGPT aided in <a href="https://twitter.com/peakcooper/status/1639716833895886850?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E1639716833895886850%7Ctwgr%5Efbf5d5d9eb00c364dec2e00263cda7e9a9b96829%7Ctwcon%5Es1_&#x26;ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Feconomictimes.indiatimes.com%2Fnews%2Fnew-updates%2Fchatgpt-saves-dogs-life-gives-correct-diagnosis-that-even-vet-could-not-identify%2Farticleshow%2F99053583.cms">saving a dog’s life by making a correct diagnosis</a> of the blood test results.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Data maybe limited to a certain date but websites like Chat GPT has the ability to detect patterns. This is why it could detect the medical symptoms with more accuracy than answering abstract questions like <em>what will I do after graduation!</em> </p>
</blockquote>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Screenshot-2023-03-29-at-6.26.44-PM.png" alt="chatgpt capability"></p>
<h3>The Problem</h3>
<p>ChatGPT is not the only or the first AI-enabled chatbot. Almost hundreds of chatbots in various languages are competing with ChatGPT. However, the free version of ChatGPT <a href="https://www.washingtonpost.com/business/energy/google-faces-a-serious-threat-from-chatgpt/2022/12/07/363d2440-75f5-11ed-a199-927b334b939f_story.html">garnered 1 million subscribers</a> in one week. The momentum was so strong that people considered it a threat to Google’s search engine, tagging it as <a href="https://www.nytimes.com/2022/12/21/technology/ai-chatgpt-google-search.html"><strong>Code Red</strong></a> for Google’s search engine.</p>
<p>Despite the fact that it could detect a medical condition with absolute accuracy, cases like these are scarce. In a majority of scenarios, inaccuracies in its responses forced people to cross-check responses from external sources, unlike Google!</p>
<p>This is exactly why <a href="https://meta.stackoverflow.com/questions/421831/temporary-policy-chatgpt-is-banned">StackOverflow has banned answers from ChatGPT</a>, stating that it harms the community and people looking for <em>correct answers.</em> Infact, if you signup for ChatGPT, the platform itself will show you this prompt –</p>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Screenshot-2023-03-29-at-5.09.32-PM.png" alt="chatgpt signup"></p>
<p>Probably this is the reason why the tool has its limitations listed officially.</p>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Screenshot-2023-03-29-at-5.13.12-PM.png" alt="chatgpt limitations"></p>
<p>Everything seems to be leading up to the single fact –</p>
<blockquote>
<p>AI has a long way to go. ChatGPT has a lot of training to do!</p>
<p>Be it any situation, a Language Learning Model can replicate human conversations but it will never be able to replicate human emotions or the <em>prose</em> like conversations.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Saying <strong>never</strong> may be too much, especially when deep learning enthusiasts continuously study the <a href="https://fastdatascience.com/how-similar-are-neural-networks-to-our-brains/">human brain’s and neural networks’ similarities and dissimilarities</a>.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Also Read: <a href="https://www.analytixlabs.co.in/blog/what-is-perceptron/">What is Perceptron – The Founding Element of Neural Networks</a></p>
</blockquote>
<p>As it happens everywhere, ChatGPT dug up the archives for people to see other tools competing in a similar domain.</p>
<p>ChatGPT triggered the <em>need to have an AI tool</em>. While it trended, people looked up to other alternatives that are more polished and did their job better.</p>
<p>Not just this, tech giants joined the race to churn out their own versions of ChatGPT or, as we call it – <strong>ChatGPT Alternatives</strong>.</p>
