</ul>
', 'Data Analytics', ARRAY['Data Analytics', 'Python']::text[], 'Beginner', '23 min read', 'al-editorial', 'https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/Cover-Image-1-2.jpg', 'How to Perform Data Analysis using Python - A Case Study With Sales Data [Codes Included]', 'Published', '2024-09-18T13:24:05.000Z'::timestamptz, '2026-02-04T09:20:03.000Z'::timestamptz, '{"canonicalUrl":"https://www.analytixlabs.co.in/blog/data-analytics-with-python/","noIndex":true,"metaTitle":"How to Perform Data Analysis using Python - A Case Study With Sales Data [Codes Included]","metaDesc":"Data Analytics with Python: Learn essential techniques & best practices to enhance your data-driven decision-making with our guide."}'::jsonb, '{}'::text[], '', '{}'::jsonb, '{}'::jsonb, '{"entityTags":["Data Analytics","Python","general"],"enabled":true}'::jsonb, '{}'::jsonb, '{"qa":true,"faqSchema":true,"moderation":"auto"}'::jsonb, '{"showLeadGen":false,"showNextSteps":false,"showCourseCta":false,"showRightSidebar":true}'::jsonb),
('How to Become a Data Architect - Role, Salary, and Learning Roadmap', 'data-architect-skills', 'Data Architect Skills: Learn the necessary skills you need to begin your Data Architect journey, exploring various roles in the field!', '<p>Imagine building a house without an architect or a blueprint—it sounds chaotic, right? Just as an architect designs a sturdy, functional home, a data architect transforms data management chaos into clarity by creating a cohesive plan for an organization’s data systems.</p>
<p>Data architects design scalable, efficient systems to ensure smooth data flow and alignment with business goals. They create data models, maintain data accuracy and security, and now also build architectures for advanced analytics and AI-driven insights.</p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong><em>Data architect employment is projected to grow <a href="https://www.bls.gov/opub/mlr/2023/article/occupational-projections-overview-2021-31.htm">9%</a> from 2021 to 2031.</em></strong></p>
</blockquote>
<p>The scope for data architect skills is increasing across industries as organizations increase their reliance on data for decision-making. This article will describe a data architect job description detailing data architect salary in India and the skills needed to grab an opportunity. By the end, you’ll have a clear roadmap to becoming a data architect in India.</p>
<h2><strong>Core Data Architect Roles and Responsibilities</strong></h2>
<p>Data architect roles and responsibilities include keeping all data frameworks efficient, secure, and aligned with business objectives. Here are the key data architect responsibilities: </p>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/Data-Architect-Role-and-Responsibilities-02-1-scaled-e1730795816586.jpg" alt="responsibilities of data architect"></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Data Modeling:</strong> Develops conceptual, logical, and physical data models for efficient storage and retrieval.</li>
<li><strong>Data Strategy and Planning:</strong> Defines standards, policies, and procedures to ensure data consistency and accuracy across systems.</li>
<li><strong>Data Integration:</strong> Design solutions for integrating data from various sources within the organization.</li>
<li><strong>Data Security:</strong> This position ensures compliance with regulations and protects sensitive information from breaches. It implements security procedures, including access controls, encryption, and backup and recovery methods.</li>
<li><strong>Performance Optimization:</strong> Monitors system performance and implements enhancements for efficiency.</li>
<li><strong>Data Governance:</strong> Establishes policies for data management, usage, and quality control.</li>
</ul>
<p>Want to Become a Data Architect? Start here</p>
<p>Data Architects always begin with other data roles like data scientist, analyst, or engineer. Enroll in our signature <a href="https://www.analytixlabs.co.in/courses">data science and analytics courses</a> to work up to the data architect role.</p>
<p>Learn the data concepts and master database management so you can begin your journey to becoming a data architect.</p>
<p>Experience end-to-end learning covering industry-relevant curriculums and projects and dedicated support in career and placement. Start your customized learning journey with AnalytixLabs.</p>
<p>Explore our ongoing courses here:</p>
<ul>
<li><a href="https://www.analytixlabs.co.in/data-science-specialization-course">Data Science Certification Course</a></li>
<li><a href="https://www.analytixlabs.co.in/pg-in-data-analytics">Data Analytics Bootcamp</a></li>
<li><a href="https://www.analytixlabs.co.in/big-data-analytics-hadoop-spark-training-course-online">Certified Big Data Engineering Course</a></li>
</ul>
<p>Have a question? <a href="https://www.analytixlabs.co.in/contact-us">Connect with us here</a>. Follow us on social media for regular data updates and course help.</p>
<h2>Data Architect Skills</h2>
<p>The role of a data architect is crucial for the success of businesses. Here are some essential data architect skills you must have:</p>
<h3><strong>Technical Skills for Data Architect Role</strong></h3>
<p>Mastery of various technologies and tools enables architects to design effective data systems. The following skills help them address complex data challenges and implement innovative solutions:</p>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/Data-Architect-Role-and-Responsibilities-03.jpg" alt="technical skills for data architect"></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Database Management:</strong> Proficiency in <a href="https://www.analytixlabs.co.in/blog/sql-for-data-analysis/">SQL</a>, NoSQL, and cloud databases like AWS or Azure.</li>
<li><strong>Data Modeling Tools:</strong> Familiarity with tools such as ERwin or Microsoft Visio for modeling.</li>
<li><strong>Programming Languages:</strong> Knowledge of <a href="https://www.analytixlabs.co.in/blog/data-analytics-with-python/">Python</a> or R for data manipulation and analysis.</li>
<li><strong>Big Data Technologies:</strong> Understanding of Hadoop, Spark, or similar frameworks for large datasets.</li>
</ul>
<blockquote>
<p>Also read: <a href="https://www.analytixlabs.co.in/blog/big-data-technologies/">Big Data Technologies That Drive Our World</a></p>
</blockquote>
<h3><strong>Soft Skills for Data Architect Role</strong></h3>
<p>Soft skills are equally crucial for a data architect’s success. These enhance collaboration and communication within teams and across departments. You should develop the following vital soft skills as an aspiring data architect:</p>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/Data-Architect-Role-and-Responsibilities-04.jpg" alt="soft skills for data architect"></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Communication Skills:</strong> Conveying technical concepts to non-technical stakeholders is essential in a data architect’s role.</li>
<li><strong>Collaboration:</strong> Working effectively with cross-functional teams to align data strategies with business goals requires collaboration and teamwork.</li>
<li><strong>Problem-solving:</strong> Strong analytical skills to analyze complex data sets and design efficient solutions.</li>
<li><strong>Adaptability:</strong> Willingness to learn new technologies and methodologies to keep up with the field’s evolving needs.</li>
<li><strong>Leadership Skills: To be successful in</strong> senior roles, you must motivate and inspire team members, delegate tasks well, and resolve conflicts.</li>
<li><strong>Analytical Thinking:</strong> Data architects must be able to think critically and analyze complex datasets to identify patterns, trends, and insights to design efficient databases.</li>
</ul>
<blockquote>
<p>Also read: <a href="https://www.analytixlabs.co.in/blog/problem-solving-skills/">Why Problem Solving Skills are Important for Data Professionals?</a></p>
</blockquote>
<h2><strong>Types of Data Architects and their Specializations</strong></h2>
<p>Data architect roles and responsibilities can be categorized into different types based on their specific focus and expertise. Each professional specializes in various aspects of data management. Understanding these roles enhances an organization’s ability to utilize their knowledge effectively. Some common types of data architects include:</p>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/Data-Architect-Role-and-Responsibilities-05.jpg" alt="types of data architects"></p>
<h3><strong>1) Enterprise Data Architect</strong></h3>
<p>Enterprise data architects align data strategies with business objectives, working with stakeholders to match data architecture with goals. They design data models and standards to ensure consistency, accessibility, and integration across departments, facilitating better decision-making and streamlined operations.</p>
<h3><strong>2) Solutions Data Architect</strong></h3>
<p>Solutions data architects design custom data solutions that meet specific business needs. They implement technologies to address departmental or project challenges, choosing tools to create data systems that solve problems. They integrate new systems with existing infrastructures, ensuring effective and scalable solutions.</p>
<h3><strong>3) Information/Data Warehouse Architect</strong></h3>
<p>Data warehouse architects specialize in creating systems that store large volumes of historical data. They focus on optimizing the architecture for efficient data retrieval and analysis, enabling organizations to gain valuable insights. They are responsible for designing and managing data storage to support business intelligence initiatives effectively.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Also read: <a href="https://www.analytixlabs.co.in/blog/data-warehouse/">A Guide to Data Warehouse: Definition, Concepts, Types, and More</a></p>
</blockquote>
<h3><strong>4) Data Security Architect</strong></h3>
<p>Data security architects focus on safeguarding an organization’s data assets. They design security frameworks that protect sensitive information from unauthorized access and breaches. They implement policies, procedures, and technologies to ensure compliance with applicable regulations like GDPR or HIPAA and develop data encryption and access control strategies to maintain data integrity and confidentiality.</p>
<h3><strong>5) Data Integration Architect</strong></h3>
<p>Data integration architects design solutions that enable different systems to communicate and share data seamlessly. The frameworks consolidate data from various sources, making it accessible for analysis and reporting. They ensure seamless communication between systems for cohesive data usage and enhanced analytical capabilities.</p>
<h3><strong>6) Data Governance Architect</strong></h3>
<p>Data governance architects establish data management policies and standards across the organization. They create guidelines for managing the integrity and reliability of organizational data, including data access policies, usage standards, and governance practices. They also work to ensure compliance with data privacy regulations and industry best practices.</p>
<h2><strong>Career Path of a Data Architect</strong></h2>
<p>The career path of a data architect in India is structured and offers various opportunities for growth and specialization. Professionals start with foundational roles such as database administrators, data analysts, or software developers, gaining hands-on experience in data management and system design. </p>
<p>They can advance to senior data architect positions as they build their technical skills in database architecture, data modeling, and cloud technologies. Many specialize in highly demanded areas like cloud architecture, big data solutions, and security.</p>
<p>Data architect skills necessitate a blend of education, hands-on experience, and specialized expertise. Understanding these elements is essential for aspiring data architects looking to excel in this field.</p>
<p>With the rising focus on digital transformation, data architects in India can expect diverse roles in sectors like finance, e-commerce, healthcare, and IT services. Continuous learning and certifications in programming, AI, ML, and data governance enhance career prospects.</p>
<p>Let’s look at how to become a data architect in India:</p>
<h3><strong>1) Education</strong></h3>
<p>A strong technical foundation is essential for aspiring data architects. Most data engineers hold a bachelor’s degree in computer science or information technology (IT). Advanced degrees, such as a master’s, can further enhance career prospects. Specialized courses or data architect certifications, such as DAMA Certified Data Management Professional (CDMP), are also beneficial.</p>
<h3><strong>2) Data experience</strong></h3>
<p>Hands-on experience in data architect roles helps with career progression. Aspiring architects can start with entry-level positions in database administration, data analytics, or software development. You can move to more complex roles once you gain practical knowledge in SQL, ETL tools, and data warehousing.</p>
<p>Advanced roles involving more complex design and management of large-scale databases are ideal for fine-tuning your data architect skills. Work experience with various technologies, such as Hadoop, Spark, and NoSQL databases, is a valuable addition to your profile.</p>
<p>Here is the data architect job description for various roles:</p>
<h4><strong>a) Entry-level Data Architect Roles</strong></h4>
<ul>
<li><strong>Data Analyst:</strong> Focuses on data interpretation and reporting.</li>
<li><strong>Database Administrator:</strong> Manages databases and ensures their performance.</li>
<li><strong>Software Developer:</strong> Writes code and develops applications that interact with databases.</li>
</ul>
<h4><strong>b) Mid-level Data Architect Roles</strong></h4>
<ul>
<li><strong>Data Engineer:</strong> Builds and maintains data pipelines.</li>
<li><strong>Business Intelligence Developer:</strong> Works on data visualization and reporting tools.</li>
<li><strong>Data Warehouse Architect:</strong> Designs and manages data warehouses.</li>
</ul>
<h4><strong>c) Senior Data Architect Roles</strong></h4>
<ul>
<li><strong>Senior Data Engineer:</strong> Specializes in big data technologies like Hadoop, Spark, and NoSQL databases.</li>
<li><strong>Lead Data Architect:</strong> Oversees the design and implementation of complex data solutions. </li>
</ul>
<h3><strong>3) Projects and Assignments</strong></h3>
<p>Working on various data architect projects and assignments helps you build a strong portfolio and showcase your skills as a data architect. Projects involving data modeling, integration, or security can enhance practical understanding. These experiences help demonstrate your proficiency in problem-solving, system design, and project management to potential employers.</p>
<h4><strong>a) Hands-On Experience</strong></h4>
<p>Data architects can work on projects that require:</p>
<ul>
<li>Designing data models to support business applications.</li>
<li>Implementing data integration solutions across various platforms.</li>
<li>Developing strategies for data governance and security.</li>
</ul>
<h4><strong>b) Team Collaborations</strong></h4>
<p>Data architects must collaborate with cross-functional teams, including data engineers, business analysts, and IT personnel. It helps them understand business requirements and translate them into technical specifications. Working on collaborative projects improves communication skills and business acumen.</p>
<h4><strong>c) Portfolio Development</strong></h4>
<p>Build a portfolio to showcase your completed projects and demonstrate your expertise to potential employers. You may include the following to create an impressive portfolio:</p>
<ul>
<li>Case studies of successful data architecture implementations.</li>
<li>Contributions to open-source projects or personal projects demonstrating database design or data integration skills.</li>
</ul>
<h3><strong>4) IT Implementation Experience</strong></h3>
<p>Experience in IT implementation helps you understand how data systems operate within organizations. You must learn to align business processes with data architecture and organizational goals. Understanding the technologies in an organization’s IT ecosystem and their integration capabilities helps build efficient systems.</p>
<p>IT implementation experience involving scalable and high-performance systems improves your data architect skills. Working on data warehousing, cloud migration, or big data analytics projects can also help you gain knowledge in database architecture, programming, and infrastructure design.</p>
<h2><strong>Data Architect Salary in India</strong></h2>
<p>Data architect salaries in India vary depending on experience and location. Entry-level positions generally start at around <a href="https://www.glassdoor.co.in/Salaries/india-data-architect-salary-SRCH_IL.0,5_IN115_KO6,20.htm">₹9,00,000 per year</a>. However, with several years of experience, a data architect’s salary can rise to  ₹20,00,000 per annum. </p>
<p>Salaries may also depend on the data architect’s roles and responsibilities, industry, and organization size. Additionally, specialized skills and certifications can further enhance earning potential in this competitive field.</p>
<ul>
<li>
<h3><strong>Data Architect Salary in India by Location</strong></h3>
</li>
</ul>
<p>Data architect salary in India also depend on location, reflecting the cost of living and demand for specialized skills in a particular area. Metro cities like Mumbai, Delhi, Chennai, Bangalore, and Hyderabad are hubs for IT companies and have higher salaries for data architects. Location-wise, pay for data architects in the top metropolitan cities of Bangalore is <a href="https://www.payscale.com/research/IN/Job=Data_Architect/Salary/2d66d4f2/Bangalore">24,00,000/yr</a>, Delhi 20,00,000/yr, Mumbai 18,00,000/yr, and Chennai 19,00,000/yr.</p>
<ul>
<li>
<h3><strong>Data Architect Salary in India by Experience</strong></h3>
</li>
</ul>
<p>Data architect salaries in India are also based on experience level. As you progress through your career, it is recommended that you gain specific skills and certifications. Experience in various data architectures, technologies, and industries increases your salary potential.</p>
<p>The average salaries for data architects based on experience of 1-3 years are <a href="https://www.glassdoor.co.in/Salaries/india-data-architect-salary-SRCH_IL.0,5_IN115_KO6,20.htm">₹4L – ₹19.3L/yr,</a> 4-6 years is ₹10.0L₹26.8L/yr, 7-9 years is ₹16.0L – ₹30.0L/yr, and for 10-14 years is ₹20.0L – ₹32.8L/yr.</p>
<h2><strong>Data Architect Job Roles with Key Skills</strong></h2>
<p>Data architect roles and responsibilities are defined according to industry, organization size, and experience level. However, some key skills are essential to excel in data architecture. </p>
<p>Some common job roles for data architects include:</p>
<h3><strong>1) Data Engineer</strong></h3>
<p>Data engineers build and maintain the architecture for large-scale data processing. They require strong programming skills and expertise in ETL (Extract, Transform, Load) processes. </p>
<p><strong>Key Skills:</strong> ETL tools (Informatica, Talend), big data technologies (Hadoop, Spark), cloud platforms (AWS or Azure).</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Also read: <a href="https://www.analytixlabs.co.in/blog/data-engineer-resume/">How To Write A Data Engineer Resume: A Practical Guide</a></p>
</blockquote>
<h3><strong>2) Data Scientist</strong></h3>
<p>Data scientists analyze and interpret complex datasets for insights that help organizations make informed decisions. They use statistical methods, ML algorithms, and data visualization tools to process data and derive meaningful information.</p>
<p><strong>Key Skills:</strong> Statistical analysis, machine learning, data mining techniques, programming languages (Python or R).</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Also read: <a href="https://www.analytixlabs.co.in/blog/data-science-course-eligibility/">How to become a Data Scientist: Courses, Eligibility, and more</a></p>
</blockquote>
<h3><strong>3) Business Intelligence (BI) Developer</strong></h3>
<p>BI developers create analytic and reporting tools and systems for analyzing business data. They work closely with stakeholders to design dashboards and reports that support strategic decision-making.</p>
<p><strong>Key Skills:</strong> BI tools (Tableau, Qlik), data warehouse design and implementation, ETL processes.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Also read: <a href="https://www.analytixlabs.co.in/blog/business-intelligence-value-chain/">Business Intelligence Value Chain</a> </p>
</blockquote>
<h3><strong>4) Database Administrator (DBA)</strong></h3>
<p>DBAs manage databases to ensure their performance and security. They are responsible for database tuning, backup, and recovery processes.</p>
<p><strong>Key Skills:</strong> Database management systems (Oracle, MySQL), SQL database design and optimization, performance tuning.</p>
<h3><strong>5) Cloud Data Architect</strong></h3>
<p>Cloud data architects design and manage data architectures on cloud platforms. They ensure scalability, security, and efficient data workflows within cloud environments.</p>
<p><strong>Key Skills:</strong> Cloud platforms (AWS, Azure, Google Cloud), infrastructure such as code, containerization (Docker, Kubernetes), and security protocols.</p>
<h3><strong>6) Information Architect</strong></h3>
<p>Information architects focus on structuring, organizing, and labeling information systems to improve usability, accessibility, and user experience. They ensure that information is logically arranged to enhance user experience.</p>
<p><strong>Key Skills:</strong> Information modeling, user experience design, taxonomy development, metadata management.</p>
<h3><strong>7) Data Governance Specialist</strong></h3>
<p>Data governance specialists develop and implement policies for managing data quality and compliance. They define procedures for effective data management, quality, and organizational compliance.</p>
<p><strong>Key Skills:</strong> Data governance frameworks, <a href="https://www.analytixlabs.co.in/blog/data-quality-management/">data quality management</a>, compliance standards (GDPR, HIPAA), and policy development.</p>
<h2><strong>Challenges and Opportunities for Data Architects</strong></h2>
<p>The data architect’s roles and responsibilities present numerous challenges. However, they also provide substantial opportunities for growth and innovation in the field. Here are some key challenges and opportunities for data architects to consider:  </p>
<h3><strong>1) Managing Data Complexity and Volume</strong></h3>
<p>Organizations collect vast amounts of data, making complexity management crucial. Data architects must design scalable systems to handle this growth and ensure optimal performance efficiently.</p>
<h3><strong>2) Ensuring Data Security and Privacy</strong></h3>
<p>Protecting sensitive information is essential for regulatory and ethical reasons. Data architects implement robust security measures to safeguard against breaches. They maintain regulatory compliance.</p>
<h3><strong>3) Leveraging Data for Competitive Advantage</strong></h3>
<p>Organizations aim to use data strategically for business growth, and data architects enable analytics that drive informed decision-making. It helps improve the company’s competitive positioning in the market.</p>
<h3><strong>4) Driving Innovation through Advanced Technologies</strong></h3>
<p>Integrating AI and ML into data architecture opens new avenues for innovation. Data architects can use design-efficient data architectures to drive business growth and create new opportunities.</p>
<h2><strong>Data Architect vs. Other Data Roles</strong></h2>
<p>The data architect job description overlaps responsibilities with other data roles, but they serve different purposes. Here is a comparison of data architect roles and responsibilities with other data jobs.</p>
<ul>
<li>
<h3><strong>Data Architect vs. Data Engineer</strong></h3>
</li>
</ul>
<p>Data engineers build and maintain data infrastructure, while data architects design and manage the architecture. A data engineer focuses on the technical implementation and optimization of data pipelines, whereas a data architect ensures that the overall architecture aligns with business goals and supports decision-making.</p>
<p>Here is a comparison of Data Architect vs. Data Engineer:</p>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/Data-Architect-Role-and-Responsibilities-06.jpg" alt="data architect vs data engineer"></p>
<ul>
<li>
<h3><strong>Data Architect vs. Data Scientist</strong></h3>
</li>
</ul>
<p>A data scientist uses statistical models and ML algorithms to analyze complex datasets and extract insights. On the other hand, a data architect designs systems using AI and ML for data-driven decision-making. Data architects build the infrastructure for data scientists to work on, while data scientists focus on deriving insights from data.</p>
<p>Here is a tabular comparison of Data Architect vs. Data Scientist:</p>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/Data-Architect-Role-and-Responsibilities-07.jpg" alt="data architect vs data scientist"></p>
<ul>
<li>
<h3><strong>Data Architect vs. Data Analyst</strong></h3>
</li>
</ul>
<p>A data analyst identifies trends and patterns, while a data architect designs the data storage and processing systems. Data analysts analyze existing data, whereas data architects focus on designing future-proof systems to manage increasing amounts of data.</p>
<p>Here is a tabular comparison of Data Architect vs. Data Analyst:</p>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/Data-Architect-Role-and-Responsibilities-08.jpg" alt="data architect vs data analyst"></p>
<h2><strong>Emerging Trends in Data Architecture</strong></h2>
<p>As data management becomes complex, several key trends are shaping the future of data architecture. These trends reflect technological advancements, business needs shifts, and data governance’s increasing importance. Here are the emerging trends in data architecture that you should look out for:</p>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/Data-Architect-Role-and-Responsibilities-09.jpg" alt="emerging trends in data architecture"></p>
<h3><strong>1) Real-Time Analytics</strong></h3>
<p>Modernization of data architectures supports real-time analytics. <a href="https://psico-smart.com/en/blogs/blog-the-impact-of-realtime-data-analytics-on-business-performance-metrics-167845">79%</a> of organizations have adopted real-time analytics to analyze data as it is generated instead of relying on batch processing. These organizations have also reported 15% revenue growth.</p>
<h3><strong>2) AI and Machine Learning in Data Architecture</strong></h3>
<p>Integrating <a href="https://www.analytixlabs.co.in/blog/ai-tools-for-data-analysis/">AI</a> and <a href="https://www.analytixlabs.co.in/blog/supervised-and-unsupervised-learning/">ML</a> into data architecture enables organizations to automate processes effectively. Data architectures need to be designed to integrate these technologies seamlessly. Companies invest in advanced frameworks supporting AI and ML capabilities for better decision-making.</p>
<h3><strong>3) Distributed Architectures</strong></h3>
<p>Implementing distributed architectures is gaining traction. This approach allows organizations to utilize multiple platforms for data processing, enhancing flexibility and reducing access times. Companies are expected to adopt established distributed architecture models cautiously, focusing on high data quality while managing technology costs.</p>
<h3><strong>4) Data Fabric and Data Mesh Concepts</strong></h3>
<p>Data fabric and data mesh architectures are emerging to eliminate data silos and enhance integration across platforms. Data fabric offers a unified layer for seamless data access across cloud and on-premises environments, while data mesh decentralizes data management, empowering teams closest to it. These architectures make organizations more agile.</p>
<h3><strong>5) Data Privacy and Compliance Regulations</strong></h3>
<p>Governments are enacting stricter data privacy laws and regulations to protect consumer data. Organizations must ensure compliance while developing data architectures. Data architects must collaborate with legal teams to implement robust governance frameworks.</p>
<h3><strong>6) Cloud-Native Architectures</strong></h3>
<p>Cloud-native architectures utilize microservices and containers to build scalable, flexible, cost-effective systems. These architectures also facilitate easy integration with AI and ML tools.</p>
<h2><strong>Conclusion</strong></h2>
<p>Data architecture is a high-demand skill today and in the years to come. As organizations collect and generate more data, the need for effective data architectures will continue to rise.</p>
<p>Data architects can create robust and efficient business systems by staying updated on the latest data architecture trends and technologies. So, it is essential for aspiring data architects to continuously upgrade and adapt to new technologies to excel in this field.</p>
<h2><strong>FAQs</strong></h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>What is the primary role of a data architect?</strong></li>
</ul>
<p>A data architect’s primary role includes developing data models, setting standards, and ensuring data integrity. They work with stakeholders to align data strategies with business goals and ensure efficient data flow across systems.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>What specific database technologies should a data architect be familiar with?</strong></li>
</ul>
<p>A data architect should be familiar with various database technologies, including relational databases like MySQL and PostgreSQL. Knowledge of NoSQL databases such as MongoDB and Cassandra is essential. Additionally, familiarity with cloud-based databases like Amazon RDS and Google BigQuery is becoming necessary for modern data architecture solutions.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>How important is communication and collaboration for a data architect?</strong></li>
</ul>
<p>Data architects must effectively communicate complex technical concepts to non-technical stakeholders. Collaborating with cross-functional teams ensures the data architecture meets the needs of various departments.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>What certifications or degrees are helpful for a data architect?</strong></li>
</ul>
<p>Helpful certifications for a data architect include those offered by AWS, Microsoft Azure, and Google Cloud. A computer science or IT degree provides foundational knowledge. Additionally, certifications in database management, big data technologies, and enterprise architecture enhance credibility and expertise in the field.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>How is AI and ML impacting the role of a data architect?</strong></li>
</ul>
<p>AI and machine learning significantly impact data architects by adding new complexities and advanced capabilities such as natural language processing (NLP), complex pattern identification, and image recognition. They must now design systems that can handle unstructured data, support advanced analytics, and process data in real time.</p>
<p>Related Reading Resources</p>
<ul>
<li><a href="https://www.analytixlabs.co.in/blog/data-analyst-vs-data-scientist/">Data Analyst vs Data Scientist: Which career option to choose in 2024?</a></li>
<li><a href="https://www.analytixlabs.co.in/blog/data-engineer-vs-data-scientist/">Data Engineer vs. Data Scientist – A Comparative Study</a></li>
<li><a href="https://www.analytixlabs.co.in/blog/data-science-bootcamp/">Why You Should Opt For Data Science Bootcamps in India?</a></li>
</ul>
', 'Data Science', ARRAY['Data Science']::text[], 'Beginner', '15 min read', 'al-editorial', 'https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/Data-Architect-Role-and-Responsibilities-01-721x515-1.jpg', 'How to Become a Data Architect - Role, Salary, and Learning Roadmap', 'Published', '2024-11-06T05:51:22.000Z'::timestamptz, '2026-02-04T08:59:19.000Z'::timestamptz, '{"canonicalUrl":"https://www.analytixlabs.co.in/blog/data-architect-skills/","noIndex":true,"metaTitle":"How to Become a Data Architect - Role, Salary, and Learning Roadmap","metaDesc":"Data Architect Skills: Learn the necessary skills you need to begin your Data Architect journey, exploring various roles in the field!"}'::jsonb, '{}'::text[], '', '{}'::jsonb, '{}'::jsonb, '{"entityTags":["Data Science","general"],"enabled":true}'::jsonb, '{}'::jsonb, '{"qa":true,"faqSchema":true,"moderation":"auto"}'::jsonb, '{"showLeadGen":false,"showNextSteps":false,"showCourseCta":false,"showRightSidebar":true}'::jsonb),
('How to Clean Data in Microsoft Excel: A Step-by-Step Illustrated Guide', 'data-cleaning-in-excel', 'Data Cleaning in Excel - A Comprehensive Step-by-Step Guide for Beginners to Transform Raw Data into Actionable Insights!', '<p>Microsoft Excel is more than spreadsheets and numbers. For data analysts and scientists, it’s a go-to tool that makes exploring, cleaning, processing, and analyzing data easy. It is the starting point for professionals looking to explore the world of data as it lays down the basics that can open doors to more advanced analysis techniques.</p>
<p>This article will explore how MS Excel can be used for data exploration, analysis, and, most importantly, cleaning. The primary focus will, therefore, be on the various data-cleaning techniques in Excel. Before we go there, let’s understand the role of data cleaning in data analysis.</p>
<h2>Why is Data Cleaning Important for Data Analysis?</h2>
<p><a href="https://www.analytixlabs.co.in/blog/minimize-dirty-data/">Data cleaning</a> is critical in almost all data analysis processes. A lack of data cleaning can cause data to have several impurities that can adversely impact the insights gained from it, leading the stakeholders to make wrong decisions. Therefore, data cleaning is crucial to ensure that the information in the data is relevant and accurate.</p>
<p>Data cleaning doesn’t happen in isolation and is often accompanied by various preprocessing steps that enhance data quality and efficiency. Analyzing data can take a lot of time, and if it is properly cleaned and processed, the effectiveness of the analytical tools can be improved. </p>
<p>Let’s have a look at the key data quality issues that are addressed through data cleaning techniques. </p>
<h3><strong>Common Data Quality Issues</strong></h3>
<p>Data can consist of many issues. The most common ones are-</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Inconsistent Format</strong>: It can occur when, for example, the date is in incorrect format, the column of a data has an incorrect data type, or the categories of a column are inconsistent, which causes issues during data aggregation, comparison, analysis, etc.</li>
<li><strong>Missing Values</strong>: While incomplete data can come up for various reasons, it can stunt the analytical potential of the data.</li>
<li><strong>Duplicates</strong>: Sometimes, records can appear multiple times, which can cause skewed analytical results, longer processing time, etc.</li>
<li><strong>Outliers</strong>: Outliers are values that significantly deviate from the data distribution. They can harm several key statistical measures, such as mean, leading to erroneous calculations.</li>
</ol>
<p>While there can be many more issues (such as incorrect data, typos, etc.), the ones mentioned above are the key ones and need the most attention. </p>
<p>Struggling with datasets?</p>
<p>Explore our signature <strong>data science and analytics courses in collaboration with <em>Electronics &#x26; ICT Academy, IIT Guwahati</em></strong>, and master your skills in excel, data analysis, and beyond. Gain hands-on experience with industry-relevant skills and begin the learning!</p>
<ul>
<li>Explore our <a href="https://www.analytixlabs.co.in/pg-in-data-analytics/">Data Analytics</a> and other <a href="https://www.analytixlabs.co.in/courses">ongoing courses here</a>.</li>
</ul>
<p>Have a question? <a href="https://www.analytixlabs.co.in/contact-us">Connect with us here</a>. Follow us on social media for regular data updates and course help.</p>
<p>Now, let’s discuss Excel and how it can help solve the abovementioned issues.</p>
<h3><strong>Can You Use Excel to Clean Data?</strong></h3>
<p><a href="https://www.microsoft.com/en/microsoft-365/excel">MS Excel</a> has great data-cleaning capabilities due to the various data-cleaning Excel formulas and tools it provides to the user. It offers Conditional Formatting to highlight different issues with data (such as outliers, duplicates, etc.).</p>
<p>In contrast, data-cleaning Excel functions and formulas like TRIM, PROPER, and SUBSTITUTE allow users to standardize and clean data. In addition, robust data cleaning tools in Excel, like PivotTables and Data Analysis, allow users to summarize and analyze data effectively.</p>
<p>To better understand Excel’s capabilities, let’s put it to use and explore some data-cleaning examples in Excel.</p>
<h2>How to Analyze Data Using Excel?</h2>
<p>Several data-cleaning Excel functions and tools allow you to explore and process data easily.</p>
<p><strong>Note:</strong> <strong><em>We have used</em></strong> <strong><em>MS Excel 2016</em></strong> <strong><em>for demonstration purposes</em></strong>.</p>
<p>To demonstrate Excel’s capabilities, we will use <strong>credit risk data</strong> (as shown below) that contains information about bank customers, their credit scores, and their loan approval status.</p>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/image58-copy.jpg" alt="credit risk dataset excel">
<em>Credit Risk Data for Data Cleaning Demonstration</em></p>
<p>We will use this data to clean data. However, before cleaning data in an Excel spreadsheet, we will analyze <a href="https://www.analytixlabs.co.in/blog/exploratory-data-analysis-in-python/">exploratory data</a> and identify the key issues.</p>
<h3><strong>Basic Data Exploration</strong></h3>
<p>The first step is to understand the data at hand. The following steps can help you do that using Excel.</p>
<h4><strong>1) Sorting by Custom Lists</strong></h4>
<p>You can sort the data using any particular column to understand it. For example, if you want to view the data such that it is sorted by the state column, then-</p>
<ul>
<li>Step 1: Select the column “State”.</li>
<li>Step 2: Go to the ‘Home’ Tab >> ‘Editing group’</li>
<li>Step 3: Select ‘Sort and Filter’</li>
<li>Step 4: Select ‘Sort A-Z’</li>
</ul>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/image61-copy.jpg" alt="sorting dataset excel"></p>
<ul>
<li>Step 5: Select ‘Expand the selection’</li>
</ul>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/image60-copy.jpg" alt="sorting dataset in excel"></p>
<ul>
<li>Step 6: Click ‘Sort’</li>
</ul>
<p>All the data is sorted now based on the “State” column.</p>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/image63-copy.jpg" alt="sorting dataset in excel"></p>
<p>Just in case you want to organize the data based on a customer list, then you could do the same by following these steps-</p>
<ul>
<li>Step 1: Select the data</li>
<li>Step 2: Go to ‘Data Tab’ → ‘Sort and Filter’ group</li>
<li>Step 3: Select the ‘Sort’ dialog and choose the column you want to sort (“State” in our case)</li>
<li>Step 4: Under the ‘Order’ column, choose Custom List.</li>
<li>Step 5: Create or select a custom list (e.g., in our case, we will manually enter state abbreviations in the desired order) and click ‘OK’  </li>
</ul>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/image62-copy.jpg" alt="sorting dataset in excel"></p>
<ul>
<li>Step 6: Click ‘OK’ to apply the custom sorting.</li>
</ul>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/image66-copy.jpg" alt="sorting dataset in excel"></p>
<p>The data is now sorted according to the customer order we provided.</p>
<p><em><strong>P.S. We will sort it to the original form for the next function.</strong></em></p>
<h4><strong>2) Filtering Data</strong></h4>
<p>If you want to view data based on a particular criteria, such as viewing records of customers belonging to California, then you can do it by applying filters to specific columns-</p>
<ul>
<li>Step 1: Select the Data Range (select the entire dataset in our case)</li>
<li>Step 2: Go to ‘Data Tab’ → ‘Sort &#x26; Filter’ group >> Click on the ‘Filter’ button (flask-shaped)</li>
<li>Step 3: Click the drop-down arrow in the column header you want to filter (in our case it is “State”)</li>
<li>Step 4: Select Criteria: Choose specific values or use options like Text Filters or Number Filters (choose Text Filters, select and provide “CA”)</li>
</ul>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/image64-copy-e1729149502722.jpg" alt="filtering data in excel"></p>
<ul>
<li>Step 5: Click ‘OK’ to apply the filter</li>
</ul>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/image65-copy.jpg" alt="filtering data in excel"></p>
<p>The data now only has records where the state is CA.</p>
<h4><strong>3) Conditional Formatting</strong></h4>
<p>To help you understand the data better, Excel provides conditional formatting that highlights cells that fulfill a specific condition. For example, we highlight cells with a loan amount between 10 and 30 thousand.</p>
<ul>
<li>Step 1: Select the Loan Amount Column (you can select the range of cells too)</li>
<li>Step 2: Go to ‘Home’ Tab → Conditional Formatting (under ‘Styles’ group) → ‘Highlight Cells Rules’</li>
<li>Step 3: Choose ‘Between’</li>
<li>Step 4: Enter the lower and upper bounds (e.g., in our case, it’s between 10,000 and 30,000)</li>
<li>Step 5: Select ‘Formatting Style’ (select red as a fill color) and click ‘OK’.</li>
</ul>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/image67-copy.jpg" alt="conditional formatting in excel"></p>
<p>Conditional formatting is a powerful tool. By altering step 3, you can highlight cells with specific text, duplicates, etc. </p>
<h3><strong>How to Identify Data Types and Inconsistencies?</strong></h3>
<p>Once you have a brief idea about the data, the next stage is to identify its key issues, which will help you clean the data in an Excel spreadsheet. The key issues include incorrect data types, empty values, and other inconsistencies.</p>
<h4><strong>1) Check for Incorrect Formatting or Data Types</strong></h4>
<p>Columns pertain to specific data types such as text, numbers, dates, etc. However, if they are stored in incorrect format, they can cause problems when performing various data manipulation-related operations.</p>
<p>Therefore, it becomes critical to identify those cells where the format is incorrect so that any erroneous analytical insights can be avoided. In our dataset, the Credit Score column is not of numeric data type, indicating that there might be an incorrect formatting issue. We will perform the following steps to identify the cells causing the issue.</p>
<ul>
<li>Step 1: Select the column with formatting issues (it is “Credit Score” for me)</li>
<li>Step 2: Go to the ‘Home’ Tab → under the ‘Styles’ group, select ‘Conditional Formatting’ → ‘New Rule’</li>
</ul>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/image68-copy.jpg" alt="checking incorrect formatting or data types in excel"></p>
<ul>
<li>Step 3: In the New Formatting Rule dialog, choose the “Use a formula to determine which cells to format” option</li>
<li>Step 4: Enter the following formula to detect text in a numeric column: <em>=ISTEXT(C1)</em> (entering C1 as “Credit Score” is in the C column).</li>
<li>Step 5: Click ‘Format’, choose a color (we will choose red in our case) to highlight the cells, and then click ‘OK’.</li>
</ul>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/image69-copy.jpg" alt="checking incorrect formatting or data types in excel"></p>
<ul>
<li>Step 6: Click ‘OK’ again to apply the rule.</li>
</ul>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/image70-copy.jpg" alt="checking incorrect formatting or data types in excel"></p>
<p>Once done, the cells that contain text get highlighted, allowing you to treat them (either by deleting such cells or entering the correct numerical values).</p>
<h4><strong>2) Flagging Blanks or Null Values</strong></h4>
<p>Incomplete data can hinder your analysis, so it’s essential to identify those cells that contain blanks or null values. Conditional Formatting again comes in handy here as it allows you to highlight such cells.</p>
<ul>
<li>Step 1: Select the entire dataset</li>
<li>Step 2: Go to Home Tab → under ‘Styles’ select ‘Conditional Formatting’ → ‘New Rule’</li>
<li>Step 3: Choose ‘Format only cells that contain’</li>
<li>Step 4: In the first drop-down, select ‘Blanks’</li>
<li>Step 5: Select ‘Choose Formatting’ and pick a fill color (we picked yellow) to highlight blank cells.</li>
</ul>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/image71-copy.jpg" alt="flagging blanks or null values in excel"></p>
<ul>
<li>Step 6: Click ‘OK’.</li>
</ul>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/image72-copy.jpg" alt="flagging blanks or null values in excel"></p>
<p>This allows you to find all the empty cells.</p>
<h4><strong>3) Flagging Outliers</strong></h4>
<p>Outliers are abnormally large or small values. There are numerous ways of identifying them. Below, you will identify the outliers in the “Loan Amount” column using the IQR (inter-quartile) method.</p>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/image73-copy.jpg" alt="flagging outliers in excel"></p>
<ul>
<li>Step 1: Calculate the Quartiles (1st quartile (Q1) and 3rd quartile (Q3)) in an empty cell by using the following formula.</li>
</ul>
<p>>Q1: <em>=QUARTILE(D:D, 1)</em> (using D:D as “Loan Amount” is in the D column in our data).</p>
<p>>Q3: <em>=QUARTILE(D:D, 3)</em></p>
<ul>
<li>Step 2: Calculate the IQR in another cell by using the formula: <em>=Q3 – Q1</em> (Q3 and Q1 cell references are L3 and L2 in our case)</li>
<li>Step 3: Determine Outlier Boundaries by using the following formula</li>
</ul>
<ol>
<li> Lower Bound: <em>=Q1 – 1.5 * IQR</em> (Q1 and IQR cell references are L2 and L4 respectively)</li>
<li>Upper Bound: <em>=Q3 + 1.5 * IQR</em> (Q3 and IQR cell references are L3 and L4 respectively)</li>
</ol>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/image74-copy.jpg" alt="flagging outliers in excel"></p>
<ul>
<li>Step 4: Flag the Outliers by using Conditional Formatting:</li>
</ul>
<p>>Select the cells containing the loan amount values</p>
<p>>Go to ‘Home’ Tab → ‘Conditional Formatting’ → ‘New Rule’</p>
<p>>Select ‘Use a Formula to determine which cells to format’</p>
<p>>Enter the formula for highlighting lower outliers</p>
<p>[<em>=D2 &#x3C; $L$6</em> (here $L$6 is the cell reference containing the Lower Bound value)]</p>
<p>Choose a color to highlight the outliers (we will choose blue)</p>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/image45-copy.jpg" alt="flagging outliers in excel"></p>
<ul>
<li>Step 5: Repeat Step 4 but with the following formula and a different color to highlight upper outliers-</li>
</ul>
<p><em>=D2 &#x3C; $L$7</em> (here $L$7 is the cell reference containing the Upper Bound value)</p>
<p>We choose the color red to highlight upper outliers</p>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/image46-copy.jpg" alt="flagging outliers in excel"></p>
<h4><strong>4) Performing Consistency Checks</strong></h4>
<p>Another issue with data can be inconsistent values. This happens especially in categorical data where data is not provided uniformly. For example, labels can sometimes be abbreviated in different cases, etc.</p>
<p>To demonstrate this, you will consider the “State” column, which should have certain state names in an abbreviated format, and use Excel’s Data Validation option to identify inconsistent cells.</p>
<ul>
<li>Step 1:  Select the cells with state values (in our case, it starts from G2 down to the last data row)</li>
<li>Step 2: Go to the ‘Data’ Tab → under the ‘Data Tools’ group, select ‘Data Validation’ → ‘Data Validation’</li>
<li>Step 3: In the ‘Settings’ tab, under the ‘Allow’ option, choose ‘List’ and enter valid state abbreviations (e.g., NY,CA,TX,FL,IL,NJ,PA,OH) as the allowed values in the ‘Source’ box.</li>
</ul>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/image47-copy.jpg" alt="checking inconsistent checks in excel"></p>
<ul>
<li>Step 4: Click ‘OK’</li>
</ul>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/image48-copy.jpg" alt="checking inconsistent checks in excel"></p>
<ul>
<li>Step 5: After setting data validation, return to the ‘Data Tab’</li>
<li>Step 6: Click on ‘Data Validation’ → ‘Circle Invalid Data’</li>
</ul>
<p>Excel will now circle any cells that don’t match your stated abbreviations. This allows you to identify entries like “new york” that are mentioned instead of “NY”. You can now manually review and correct circled entries to ensure all states are entered using abbreviations, ensuring consistency.</p>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/image49-copy.jpg" alt="checking inconsistent checks in excel"></p>
<ul>
<li>
<h3><strong>Data Cleaning</strong> </h3>
</li>
</ul>
<p>After identifying the issues, the next step is to correct them. In this section, we will provide numerous data cleaning examples in Excel by addressing the abovementioned issues and take a few more steps to clean and prepare the data further.</p>
<h4><strong>1) Removing Duplicates</strong></h4>
<p>To remove duplicates from the data, you can go through the following steps-</p>
<ul>
<li>Step 1: Select the complete Dataset (or the specific column(s) where duplicates might exist)</li>
<li>Step 2: Go to the ‘Data’ Tab → under the ‘Data Tools’ group, select ‘Remove Duplicates’</li>
<li>Step 3: In the dialog, select columns that you want to check for duplicates (e.g., we will select “Customer ID”)</li>
</ul>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/image50-copy.jpg" alt="removing duplicates in excel"></p>
<ul>
<li>Step 4: Click OK.</li>
</ul>
<p>Once done, Excel will provide a summary of duplicates found and removed.</p>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/image51-copy-e1729158839621.jpg" alt="removing duplicates in excel"></p>
<h4><strong>2) Correcting Data Inconsistencies</strong></h4>
<p>In the previous section, you found inconsistencies like “New York” being mentioned instead of “NY”. To resolve this, you can perform Find and Replace by-</p>
<ul>
<li>Step 1: Select the column where find and replace is to be performed</li>
<li>Step 2: Press Ctrl + H to open the ‘Find and Replace’ dialog box</li>
<li>Step 3: In ‘Find what’, enter the incorrect value (we will mention “new york”)</li>
<li>Step 4: Enter the correct value in ‘Replace with’ (we provide “NY”)</li>
</ul>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/image52-copy-e1729158868240.jpg" alt="correcting data inconsistencies in excel"></p>
<ul>
<li>Step 5: Click ‘Replace All’ to standardize the values</li>
</ul>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/image53-copy.jpg" alt="correcting data inconsistencies in excel"></p>
<p>You can use the same methodology to solve other issues identified earlier, such as removing text or symbols in numerical columns to convert them into the correct data type.</p>
<p>Data cleaning Excel formulas can also resolve other hidden inconsistencies in the data. These include extra spaces, incorrect cases, etc., which can also be resolved by using formulas such as <em>TRIM()</em> and <em>PROPER()</em> or <em>UPPER(),</em> respectively.</p>
<h4><strong>3) Handling Missing Values</strong></h4>
<p>Several empty cells were identified previously. To better understand the data, filling the empty cells is imperative. Many data cleaning techniques in Excel can help you resolve such issues, with one such technique being missing value imputation. Below, we perform missing value imputation using the median in the “Credit Score” column.</p>
<ul>
<li>Step 1: Calculate the Median in an empty cell by typing the following formula: <em>=MEDIAN(C:C)</em> (we use C:C as the “Credit Score” is in the C column)</li>
</ul>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/image54-copy-e1729158914711.jpg" alt="performing missing value imputation in excel"></p>
<ul>
<li>Step 2: Copy the cell with the median value (by right-clicking the cell with the median value and choosing Copy or by pressing ‘Ctrl+C’) and paste it in the same cell as values (right click 🡪‘Paste Special’ 🡪‘Paste as values’)</li>
</ul>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/image11-copy.jpg" alt="performing missing value imputation in excel"></p>
<ul>
<li>Step 3: Copy the median value (press’ Ctrl + C’ on the cell with the median value, which is now stored as a value)</li>
<li>Step 4: Select the Column with missing values (select all the cells of the column “Credit Score”)</li>
</ul>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/image12-copy.jpg" alt="performing missing value imputation in excel"></p>
<ul>
<li>Step 5: Select all of the empty cells by pressing ‘Ctrl + G’ → ‘Special’ → ‘Blanks’ → ‘OK’</li>
<li>Step 6: Paste the copied median value in all the empty cells by pressing ‘Ctrl + V’</li>
</ul>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/image13-copy.jpg" alt="performing missing value imputation in excel"></p>
<p>These steps eliminate the “Credit Score” columns’ empty cells.</p>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/image14-copy.jpg" alt="performing missing value imputation in excel"></p>
<p>We followed the same steps for the “Loan Amount” column, which had missing cells.</p>
<h4><strong>4) Outlier Capping</strong></h4>
<p>Apart from missing values, we also identified outliers in the previous section. One way to handle outliers is by capping, where values above the upper bound are capped at the upper limit, and values below the lower bound are capped at the lower limit, respectively. As you had already calculated the upper and lower bound values earlier, you can now use them to perform the capping.</p>
<ul>
<li>Step 1: Select the column next to the “Loan Amount” column and press “Ctrl + Shift + +” to add a new column.</li>
<li>Step 2: Name the new column “Loan Amount Capped.”</li>
<li>Step 3: In the first empty cell of this column, paste the following formula to cap values</li>
</ul>
<p>= IF(D2 &#x3C; $M$2, $M$2, IF(D2 > $M$3, $M$3, D2))</p>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/image15-copy.jpg" alt="outlier capping in excel"></p>
<p><strong>Note</strong>: $M$2 and $M$3 are the cell references to where the Lower Bound and Upper Bound are stored</p>
<p>This formula does the following:</p>
<p>>If the value is less than the lower bound, it sets the value to the lower bound</p>
<p>>If the value exceeds the upper bound, it sets the value to the upper bound</p>
<p>>Otherwise, it keeps the original value</p>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/image16-copy.jpg" alt="outlier capping in excel"></p>
<ul>
<li>Step 4:  Drag this formula down the column to apply the capping for all values in the “Loan Amount” column.</li>
<li>Step 5: Copy the “Loan Amount Capped” column and paste it as values on top of the same column.</li>
<li>Step 6: Delete the original Loan Amount column by selecting the column and pressing “Ctrl + -“</li>
<li>Step 7: Rename the “Loan Amount Capped” to “Loan Amount”</li>
</ul>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/image17-copy.jpg" alt="outlier capping in excel"></p>
